  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "class_subclasses",
    "file": "mruby/mrbgems/mruby-class-ext/src/class.c",
    "description": "`class_subclasses` iterates all objects via `mrb_objspace_each_objects` without protecting temporary/live objects created or referenced during iteration from GC. During this traversal, `mrb_full_gc` runs and sweeps a String object later used as a Hash key; the Hash insertion path (`obj_hash_code` -> `mrb_str_hash`) then dereferences the freed string buffer (`RSTR_PTR`), causing heap-use-after-free. Root cause is unsafe GC interaction/object lifetime handling in `class_subclasses` object-space iteration, not the hash function itself.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires Ruby code (from `mruby_fuzzer` input passed to `mrb_load_string`) that invokes `Module.subclasses`/`class_subclasses` while also creating/using objects (notably String keys in Hash operations) that remain reachable only through transient VM state during the iteration. `mrb_objspace_each_objects` in `class_subclasses` causes a full GC/sweep, freeing a string buffer; subsequent hash key hashing (`Hash#[]=` path in `hash.c`) reads that freed buffer, producing UAF."
  },
